{"path":"experimental/basic_string_view","title":"std::experimental::basic_string_view","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::</span>basic_string_view","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/basic_string_view","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The class template basic_string_view describes an object that can refer to a constant contiguous sequence of char-like objects with the first element of the sequence at position zero.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/string_view\">&lt;experimental/string_view&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> CharT, <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Traits <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/char_traits\"><span class=\"kw1275\">std::<span class=\"me2\">char_traits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> basic_string_view<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The class template <code>basic_string_view</code> describes an object that can refer to a constant contiguous sequence of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span></code>-like objects with the first element of the sequence at position zero. \n</p><p>A typical implementation holds only two members: a pointer to constant <code>CharT</code> and a size.\n</p><p>